On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:40:10 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Update the contents and commit message per new style info in CLAUDE.md.

Done in "[PATCH v2] doc: Add a guide to the patch workflow" [1]. The
guide and the commit message now use one space after each full stop.
The guide had no semicolon fragments. Runs of spaces remain only where
org needs them, in code and list indentation and in the padding that
aligns table columns.

> There should be a brief end-to-end example of prompting via email,
> processing it, providing feedback, and ultimately applying patches.

v2 adds a section, "The cycle", right after the model. It opens by
describing the system as an agentic loop with a human collaborator.
Then it walks through the hello-lab-devel request [2] in five steps,
with the commands for each:

1. You send the request and put it on the list (just commit-mail,
   advance, push).
2. The operator starts a pass with /process-email in claude, in
   ~/lab/default.jj in the jail. The pass posts the series, replies,
   and pushes to submissions.
3. The moderator takes the mail (just fetch, summary, advance, push).
4. You review by replying to the patch. The next pass posts v2 and
   answers. Steps 2 to 4 repeat.
5. You apply with just am, move trunk, push, and reply that it was
   applied.

The guide still covers only committed tooling, so step 2 shows the
skill rather than "just process-email" from "[PATCH 0/3] Add just
process-email" [3]. Once that lands, step 2 becomes a single just
command.

One correction to my reply in "[doc] Need a guide for basic operation
of the patch workflow" [4]: it cited v1 under a mistyped Message-ID.
The correct one is [5].

